.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_RESOLVE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_resolve ,
.Nm mbt_resolve_cancel
.Nd Asynchronous name resolution.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/resolve.h
.Vt int
.Fn mbt_resolve "struct mbt_ev *ev" "const char *host" "uint16_t port" "mbt_resolve_cb cb" "void *arg" "struct mbt_resolve **out"
.Vt void
.Fn mbt_resolve_cancel "struct mbt_resolve *r"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_resolve
module provides an asynchronous mechanism to resolve hostnames to IP addresses within an event loop. This allows the application to perform DNS lookups without blocking the main execution thread.
.Sh FUNCTIONS
The following functions manage asynchronous resolution:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_resolve
Initiates a name resolution request for the specified host and port. Upon completion, the provided callback is executed with the resolved address. Returns an error code on failure.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_resolve_cancel
Cancels a pending resolution request. The metadata associated with the request will be cleaned up by the event loop.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3
